  "attestation": "FC-16 batch audit fixes (auditor findings on c819e0b). M1: alembic_transfer send converts only what is not yet in Alembic's layout: a decision log part over ROLL_BYTES is cut (logParts on the joined log), one-file review records are appended to the monthly .jsonl parts while every part the folder holds is carried byte for byte (site_export verificationLines now merges; exportSite reads the log from its parts); GenChem copy (temp/genchem-update-2026-11-01, copied to /tmp): before, send refused with 5,299 'missing' records; after, 366 files, records check passes, the 7 verification parts byte-identical, LOG cut into 3 parts joining to the original, and Alembic's readCourseZip/planCourseImport (apps/web tsx, read-only) plan all 366 files with nothing left out. M2: every hidden path is left out except .alembic/handout.json and .coursewerk-host.json, named in a note. M3: slides/<x>.md with no .slides.md goes as slides/<x>.slides.md (ATTRIBUTION.md follows), named in a note and in renamed[]; Alembic's planCourseImport maps them to the chapter's slides part (before: unitPartForPath null, loose file). L1: records_check --records binds each record's path to its dispatch (verification/<dispatch>.json; wrapped lines likewise) and refuses a top-level verification/ file that is not .json/.jsonl. L2: dispatchLogEntry indexes the log's dispatch entries once per log array (WeakMap, rebuilt if the array grew): GenChem records check 4.0 s -> 2.5 s. L3: record files over 4,000,000 bytes (bring-in) / 16 MB (bring-back) are reported; page limit corrected to Alembic's MAX_UPLOAD_BYTES 4,000,000. New tests: alembic-transfer.audit (5), records-check-bound.audit (3), each failing before the fix (8/8 fail on the pre-fix sources). Full suite under lockf --test-concurrency=2: 1309/1310; the one failure (workflow.test.mjs publish: package-changed-during-run, a load-dependent skeleton check unrelated to these files) passes alone and in a full rerun of workflow.test.mjs (18/18). Reviewed every required item: requirements req.host.alembic-transfer, req.records.chain-check-bound, req.records.site-export restated to what is checked; CHANGELOG, PROCEDURE and format-contracts/deliverables.md follow; no other claim, document, template, skill or site page changes meaning.",
